{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And if a soul sins.</b> [If] he commits one of the negative commandments and did not know that it is forbidden, he shall bring a ram. The opinion of the many is that this is a suspended guilt-offering: he does not know whether he did or whether he did not do it. And the sin-offering at the beginning [of the passage]: he did not know, and afterward he knew — it is a sin-offering where he did not know that it is forbidden until he was informed. And the guilt-offering: he knew that it is forbidden but forgot, and afterward remembered. Or [it is] a suspended guilt-offering."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:40.447259474Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}